        "thought_text": "I apologize for the oversight. The current approach using a counting sort is correct in its logic, but it's inefficient for large input sizes due to the large range of possible citation counts. Instead, we can use a more efficient approach by sorting the citations in descending order and then finding the H-Index by iterating through the sorted list. This approach will be more time-efficient and avoid the issue of overcounting.",
